    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0443" n="185" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg185"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1994</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schmedeman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Christiania</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-11T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 11, 1915, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5.30 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>44. Norwegian buyers of American copper and copper wire have been informed by
                    Norwegian American line that British Government has instructed the line to
                    discontinue carrying said goods to Norway where large amounts are used and whose
                    other sources of supply are cut off. British Government demands shipment on
                    British vessels via Great Britain in which event Norwegian buyers fear that
                    goods will not reach them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schmedeman</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
